{
  "comment": "@spec ACTION-EXECUTOR-9 @spec ACTION-EXECUTOR-10. The sealed reply convention, read by every image that judges one. `envelope` states the grammar of `reply.prior`. Each vector is a connector's structured reply to a write call (`reply`, the `result` of its `side_effect_flag`) and the runner's held secret literals (`held_secrets`). `expand_ciphertext`, when present, replaces `reply.prior.ciphertext` with `fill` repeated `length` times followed by `suffix`, so a size boundary stays readable. `envelope_valid` is the grammar verdict on `reply.prior` alone (the API's `is_sealed_envelope`). `runner` is what `OutboundRedactor` does to the frame: `replay_inputs` `verbatim` means `prior`, `version` and `target` cross byte-identical, `withheld` means all three cross as null; `redacted` is the frame flag; `scrubbed` names the other `result` fields the redactor changes, and every unnamed field crosses unchanged. `worker` is the worker's recording verdict on the frame the runner emitted: `records_snapshot` true means the completion records `prior_state` as the envelope and `post_version` as `reply.version`; false means `prior_state` is null. Read by apps/api/tests/test_sealed_snapshot_reply_vector.py, apps/worker/tests/test_sealed_snapshot_reply_vector.py and runner/tests/test_sealed_snapshot_reply_vector.py, each of which rejects an unknown key; the reference connector's tests (plan task 7) read it too.",
